<title>SWITZERLAND: Ascom takes rest of venture from Ericsson.</title>
<headline>Ascom takes rest of venture from Ericsson.</headline>
<dateline>BERNE 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss telecommunications group Ascom Holding AG said it had taken over all of a previous joint venture in telepaging with Sweden's Ericsson.</p>
<p>&quot;Ascom has taken over the remaining 40 percent share held by Ericsson in Ascom Ericsson Transmission Ltd, completing the realignment of Public Networks' business to telecoms solutions and carrier access,&quot; Ascom said in a statement.</p>
<p>It did not elaborate on the acquisition terms.</p>
<p>The joint venture in on-site paging was announced in 1995 and approved by the European Commission in January 1996.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Newsroom, +41-1-631 7340</p>
